    "preamble": "Sahil Singh vs State Of Rajasthan (2024:Rj-Jd:28811) on 15 July, 2024 Author: Vinit Kumar Mathur Bench: Vinit Kumar Mathur [2024:RJ-JD:28811] HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE FOR RAJASTHAN AT JODHPUR S.B. Civil Writ Petition No. 19010/2022 1. Sahil Singh S/o Shri Amar Singh, Aged About 24 Years, By Caste Rajput Resident Of Ward No. 8 Chak 5 SSW Jhamber Tehsil And District Hanumangarh (Raj). 2. Rameshwar Meena S/o Shri Sher Singh Meena, Aged About 27 Years, By Caste Meena Resident Of Village Ranwal District Sawai Madhopur (Raj.). 3. Vinod Kumar Meena S/o Shri Shobha Ram Meena, Aged About 25 Years, By Caste Meena Resident Of Village Khajuri Kalan, Post Doongargaon Tehsil Asnawar District Jhalawar (Raj.). 4. Duda Ram Gadri S/o Shri Dev Kishan, Aged About 24 Years, By Caste Gadri Resident Of Village Bhimpura Tehsil Shapura District Bhilwara (Raj.). ----Petitioners Versus 1. State Of Rajasthan, Through Secretary, Department Of Personal, Govt. Of Rajasthan, Secretariat, Jaipur. 2. Rajasthan Public Service Commission, Ajmer, Through Its Secretary. 3. Food Safety And Standards Authority Of India, New Delhi Through Its Chief Executive Officer. ----Respondents For Petitioner(s) : Mr. Lucky Rajpurohit for Mr. Rajat Arora For Respondent(s) : Mr. Rajesh Punia HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE VINIT KUMAR MATHUR Order 15/07/2024 1. Heard learned counsel for the parties. Sahil Singh vs State Of Rajasthan (2024:Rj-Jd:28811) on 15 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/14995539/ 1 2.",
    "facts": "Accordingly, the respondents are directed to declare the withheld result of the petitioners.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the writ petition was filed on an anticipation that the degree held by the petitioners are not as per the eligibility conditions shown in the notification dated 21.10.2022. Learned counsel further submits that so far, the candidature of the petitioners has not been found to be ineligible as no orders adverse to the petitioners have been passed."
  },
